WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.147 --> 00:00:18.988
Riley gasped at Delaney's news.

2
00:00:19.008 --> 00:00:23.772
"Jordan said the Blue Demons were expanding the junior division this year!"

3
00:00:23.792 --> 00:00:29.096
"That was the original plan," Delaney replied with a sigh.

4
00:00:29.912 --> 00:00:33.013
"But unfortunately, we don't have the funds for it anymore.

5
00:00:34.393 --> 00:00:35.274
Don't worry, Riley.

6
00:00:35.554 --> 00:00:36.654
I'm sure you'll make the team.

7
00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:40.755
You're a good rider—and Jordan Clark's sister!"

8
00:00:41.855 --> 00:00:44.556
Riley wished she felt as sure as Delaney sounded.

9
00:00:45.256 --> 00:00:47.497
At the starting line, she snapped on her helmet.

10
00:00:49.598 --> 00:00:54.099
Then she eyed the track, trying to will the knots in her stomach to go away.

11
00:00:55.099 --> 00:01:00.478
Thinking about Jordan's accident had unsettled her, and Delaney's bad news didn't help one bit.

12
00:01:01.459 --> 00:01:04.862
Especially after watching Quinn, her new competition, ride the track.

13
00:01:04.882 --> 00:01:11.127
"Where your brain goes, your body will follow," she whispered to herself.

14
00:01:12.588 --> 00:01:14.930
Three more riders were ahead of Riley in line.

15
00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:19.333
Riley kept her eyes on the track, going over it again and again.

16
00:01:20.314 --> 00:01:22.356
It wasn't the toughest track she'd ever seen.

17
00:01:22.996 --> 00:01:27.000
But there were definitely tricky spots that would require serious focus.

18
00:01:28.316 --> 00:01:29.637
Riley heard another whistle.

19
00:01:29.657 --> 00:01:32.700
"That's for you, Riley!"

20
00:01:33.141 --> 00:01:33.921
Delaney called.

21
00:01:33.941 --> 00:01:37.545
"Three, two, one, go!"

22
00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:41.648
Riley pushed off.

23
00:01:42.349 --> 00:01:48.234
The dirt on the track was freshly dug—soft, but not too soft because the riders before Riley had

24
00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:49.936
already packed it down in places.

25
00:01:50.917 --> 00:01:54.260
The sun felt warm on her shoulders as she pumped the bike pedals.

26
00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.701
She needed to pick up speed and pick it up fast.

27
00:01:59.422 --> 00:02:02.243
A steady speed of 13 miles per hour was the goal.

28
00:02:04.144 --> 00:02:07.386
Riley pumped harder, letting her mind go into the "zone."

29
00:02:09.147 --> 00:02:14.530
In seconds the sounds of people and other bikes faded away, and all she could hear were her

30
00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:16.491
own tires traveling along the dirt.

31
00:02:17.091 --> 00:02:18.632
The first jump was coming up.

32
00:02:19.933 --> 00:02:24.495
Jumping a bike was a basic skill, one of the first things Riley had learned when she started

33
00:02:24.535 --> 00:02:25.276
mountain biking.

34
00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:33.197
Beginning riders, and people who didn't know anything about the sport, thought jumps were rock-star moves—dazzling tricks.

35
00:02:34.197 --> 00:02:38.440
Jumps weren't easy, but a good one was simply about timing and balance.

36
00:02:39.421 --> 00:02:44.084
Riders had to know their bikes, and know when and how to use their bodies to push the

37
00:02:44.124 --> 00:02:44.965
bike through the air.

38
00:02:46.106 --> 00:02:49.088
Jumping was definitely Riley's favorite part of the sport.

39
00:02:49.788 --> 00:02:52.090
It came naturally to her, like breathing.

40
00:02:53.471 --> 00:02:55.272
Riley pushed herself to pedal harder.

41
00:02:56.788 --> 00:03:01.471
She needed enough speed so she could stop pedaling, pull up the bike, and lift out of the

42
00:03:01.531 --> 00:03:02.672
seat at the right moment.

43
00:03:03.753 --> 00:03:06.655
Without enough speed, she wouldn't even get off the ground.

44
00:03:07.656 --> 00:03:09.197
The steps ran through her mind.

45
00:03:09.217 --> 00:03:11.358
"Keep your weight between the wheels.

46
00:03:12.439 --> 00:03:13.360
Lower your chest.

47
00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.902
Feel the force of the jump through your tires."

48
00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:19.744
She felt the front wheel hit the incline of the jump.

49
00:03:21.486 --> 00:03:24.528
Then she rose out of the seat, half-standing on the pedals.

50
00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:31.564
The bike's wheels lifted off the ground, and for a perfect moment, time stopped.

51
00:03:33.625 --> 00:03:38.769
Riley held her bike beneath her, suspended in space, the air cool and fresh on her face.

52
00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:44.693
As the bike began to drop, Riley turned her attention to the landing.

53
00:03:45.553 --> 00:03:49.576
The trick to a good landing was keeping the wheels level so they hit the ground at the

54
00:03:49.616 --> 00:03:54.620
same time—none of those fancy trick "wheelie" moves that flashy riders liked.

55
00:03:55.628 --> 00:03:59.270
They were a dangerous way to land and would cut into a rider's speed.

56
00:04:00.431 --> 00:04:03.873
Riley braced her arms and legs to absorb the force of the impact.

57
00:04:04.774 --> 00:04:06.855
Bam! A perfect landing!

58
00:04:07.975 --> 00:04:10.477
Riley headed for the straightaway and the second jump.

59
00:04:11.558 --> 00:04:14.479
She glanced at her speedometer: ten miles per hour.

60
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.180
She needed more speed.

61
00:04:18.001 --> 00:04:22.024
The next jump was just past a bend in the track, making the timing tricky.

62
00:04:23.024 --> 00:04:26.166
Riley started assessing whether she'd have to slow down on the curve.

63
00:04:27.466 --> 00:04:30.548
An image of Quinn and her flashy bike popped into her head.

64
00:04:31.609 --> 00:04:35.991
Riley would show that stuck-up new girl how good Riley's battered old bike was!

65
00:04:37.072 --> 00:04:38.572
Riley sailed into the jump.

66
00:04:40.173 --> 00:04:43.295
But this time her front wheel wobbled as she started to rise.

67
00:04:44.856 --> 00:04:49.558
Riley frantically tried to adjust her weight, to level out her wheels before they hit the ground.

68
00:04:52.019 --> 00:04:52.600
Too late.

69
00:04:53.472 --> 00:04:56.314
The back wheel hit the ground first and slid sideways.

70
00:04:58.495 --> 00:05:01.757
Then Riley came down hard, coughing and tasting dirt.

71
00:05:04.538 --> 00:05:06.399
Riley lay there, her heart racing.

72
00:05:09.201 --> 00:05:11.662
A sharp pain shot through her right foot and ankle.

73
00:05:12.883 --> 00:05:17.025
All she could think of was Jordan lying on that stretcher at the Hawk Mountain track.

74
00:05:17.045 --> 00:05:20.347
"Oh no," she murmured.

75
00:05:20.367 --> 00:05:27.334
"Riley!" By now Delaney and Sofia, another member of the Blue Demons, were running toward her.

76
00:05:30.395 --> 00:05:32.016
Sofia bent over Riley.

77
00:05:32.036 --> 00:05:34.717
"Are you okay?"

78
00:05:34.737 --> 00:05:37.999
"I Slowly Riley raised her head and blinked.

79
00:05:38.019 --> 00:05:43.281
"My ankle hurts," she said, trying to keep panic out of her voice.

80
00:05:43.301 --> 00:05:45.862
"Did I break anything?

81
00:05:45.882 --> 00:05:47.102
Am I okay?"

82
00:05:47.122 --> 00:05:50.804
"We're going to check you out," Delaney said calmly.

83
00:05:51.604 --> 00:05:52.844
"Lie still for a second."

84
00:05:54.705 --> 00:05:57.146
He pulled off her bike shoe and examined her foot.

85
00:05:57.166 --> 00:06:03.347
"Ow!" Riley said as Delaney gently moved her ankle around.

86
00:06:03.367 --> 00:06:06.908
"It hurts, but I can move it."

87
00:06:06.928 --> 00:06:11.030
"I don't think you've broken anything," Delaney said.

88
00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:14.230
"You probably have a nasty sprain, though.

89
00:06:14.911 --> 00:06:16.091
Let's see if you can get up."

90
00:06:17.311 --> 00:06:22.497
Slowly Riley hobbled to her feet, clutching Delaney and Sofia's arms for support.

91
00:06:24.158 --> 00:06:29.840
She was a mess, with dirt and grass all over her clothing, but her ankle was actually starting

92
00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:30.460
to feel better.

93
00:06:31.461 --> 00:06:33.161
She looked at the track marks in the dirt.

94
00:06:33.181 --> 00:06:37.023
"I think I dug another path out of the trail with that fall."

95
00:06:37.043 --> 00:06:43.065
"I'll be sure to put up a Caution sign," Delaney replied with a smile.

96
00:06:43.085 --> 00:06:46.247
"Let's see if you can put any weight on that ankle."

97
00:06:47.647 --> 00:06:49.388
Riley gingerly put her foot down.

98
00:06:52.056 --> 00:06:55.057
"Not so bad," she said through gritted teeth.

99
00:06:55.998 --> 00:07:00.599
Delaney and Sofia helped her to the sidelines and sat her on the grass under a tree.

100
00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:09.241
Sofia wrapped Riley's ankle with a bandage from the team's first aid kit.

101
00:07:13.022 --> 00:07:15.343
"You're going to have some epic bruises, Riley.

102
00:07:15.883 --> 00:07:18.184
You'd better get an x-ray, to be on the safe side."

103
00:07:20.488 --> 00:07:23.871
She went to find Coach Adams while Delaney called Riley's mom.

104
00:07:23.891 --> 00:07:30.417
"Your mom is on her way," Delaney said, sliding his phone back into his pocket.

105
00:07:30.437 --> 00:07:38.103
"Okay." Riley's cheeks burned with embarrassment when she saw a bunch of kids looking at her.

106
00:07:38.123 --> 00:07:40.505
"Nothing to see here!"

107
00:07:41.046 --> 00:07:42.667
she called out, forcing a laugh.

108
00:07:43.648 --> 00:07:45.530
"I'm fine.

109
00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:47.752
You can move along, people!"

110
00:07:48.956 --> 00:07:53.881
Then she lay back and closed her eyes, hoping she'd sounded as light as she'd intended.

111
00:07:53.901 --> 00:07:58.206
"What a disaster," she thought miserably.
